            <ArticleTitle>Peripheral venepuncture in infants and children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-50; quiz 52, 55-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Venepuncture can be a painful and frightening experience for children. Nurses play an active role in helping them to cope with this experience and in reducing the adverse effects of venepuncture. This article explains how infants, children and their families can be supported and cared for before, during and after venepuncture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
